Can anyone enlighten me as to why nimEigen has issues with certain rate matrices I am working with while eigen in base R appears to be happy with them?

library(nimble)

#compare eigen and nimEigen on "good" rate matrix. No problems.
k.good <- rbind(
c(-2.745826852453871147,  1.037784033000000106,  0.0000000000000000000,  0.0000000000000000000,  1.696373675000000025),
c(0.000000000000000000, -0.019121448453871134,  0.0074523039999999999,  0.0000000000000000000,  0.000000000000000000),
